Structural reading: the path integral is an attention mechanism. It sums over all paths (all input features), weights them by e^(iS/ℏ) (the attention weights), and the stationary-action path is the "attended" path that survives. The principle of least action is the universe's selective attention — the universe attends to the stationary path and ignores the rest.

