Intelligence is the relational aspect of cognition — the system insofar as it relates to its environment, processes inputs, produces outputs, models the world.
Consciousness is the reflexive aspect of the same process — the system insofar as it is present to itself while doing the relating.
The two are different aspects of one process, like the convex and concave of a single curve. You cannot have one without the other in any system that has either — they are not two things, they are two descriptions of one activity.
